FAQ = [
 ("What is the best roof rack for a 2021–2026 Chevy Tahoe?",
  "The BRIGHTLINES factory-style crossbars are the best overall roof rack for the 2021–2026 Tahoe. The title names the whole generation, including the 2025 refresh, and the bars look like they came with the truck. KINGGERI is the lockable pick, with flush side rails named in the title and a 330 lb printed rating. ROKIOTOEX Coyote prints a 220 lb figure in line with the brand-name kits. For a written 165 lb rating and a lifetime warranty, the Thule or Yakima flush-rail kit is the proof option. Check the roof and trim first: the rails are flush, the Z71 is sold as its own fit, and an RST with the Performance Edition package may have no rack at all."),
 ("Does the 2021–2026 Chevy Tahoe have raised or flush roof rails?",
  "Flush. etrailer's roof page for the 2023 Tahoe lists one roof type, \"Flush mounted rails that run front to back\", and every system on that page is a flush-rail setup. The Rack Shop sells its Tahoe kits as \"w/flush rails\". A flush rail sits on the roof along its whole length with no gap underneath, so a raised-rail tower that wraps under the rail has nothing to grab. On Amazon, the KINGGERI and ROKIOTOEX titles say \"Flush Side Rails\" outright; the EYOUHZ title says \"with Side Rails\", which is the same rail. Before you order anything, look at your own roof from the side and check that the rails are there. Edmunds' 2025 trim page says the RST Performance Edition package \"Removes roof rack\"."),
 ("Does the Tahoe Z71 need a different roof rack?",
  "The retailers treat the Z71 as its own fit. The Rack Shop sells a separate Thule setup listed for the \"2021-2026 Chevrolet Tahoe Z71 (w/flush rails)\", built on Thule Evo Flush Rail feet and Thule Fit Kit 186117, with a 165 lb maximum and a 58 in maximum bar spread, at $604.85 on sale. etrailer names the same kit, 186117 (sold there as TH95JW), for a 2022 Tahoe with flush rails, so the Z71 page is a separate listing rather than a different kit. For Thule or Yakima, have the retailer confirm the kit for your trim by VIN rather than ordering from a general Tahoe page. None of the Amazon titles here names or excludes the Z71, so a Z71 owner buying a budget set should send the seller a photo of the rail before ordering."),
 ("What is the roof load limit on a 2021–2026 Tahoe?",
  "We could not confirm a Chevrolet figure. The owner's manual is the authority, and the roof-load section is where to look. Chevrolet Accessories' own cross rail package page (part 86558288) says only that \"Load capacity varies by make, model and trim\". What we can give you is the kit ratings: The Rack Shop lists 165 lb for its Yakima SightLine kit and its Z71 Thule kit, and etrailer lists 165 lb for the Thule Evo Flush Rail feet even though the 60 in WingBar Evo bars are rated at 220 lb. The feet set the ceiling. The Amazon sets print 220 to 330 lb, which are seller bar ratings. Use the lowest of the manual, feet and bar figures, and count the bars and any box against it."),
 ("Do Tahoe crossbars fit the Suburban, Yukon and Escalade?",
  "Our vehicle data says the Suburban shares the Tahoe's roof fit, and the Amazon listings agree: the KINGGERI, EZREXPM and EYOUHZ titles name the Tahoe, Suburban, Yukon, Yukon XL or Escalade ESV together, and Chevrolet Accessories lists one cross rail package, 86558288, for the 2021–2026 Suburban and Tahoe. The BRIGHTLINES title names the Tahoe and Yukon. The roof is the same rail; the Suburban's longer body only puts more roof behind the rear bar. What does not carry over is the trim-specific fit kit on the brand-name systems, so a Yukon AT4 or a Suburban Z71 owner should ask the retailer for the kit by VIN rather than assuming the Tahoe kit."),
 ("Will a roof rack work with the Tahoe's panoramic sunroof?",
  "Yes, by the listings. The BRIGHTLINES crossbar and ski rack bundle on Amazon says \"(fit Panoramic Sunroof)\" in its title, ASG Auto Sports lists BRIGHTLINES' Tahoe crossbars as including panoramic sunroof variants, and Chevrolet Accessories describes its 86558288 cross rail package as engineered for \"full utility of your sunroof\". The bars sit on the rails above the glass line. What to check is the load, not the bars: a cargo box front edge or a bike fork mount can hang over the glass. Load the rack, then open the sunroof once while parked and watch what moves."),
 ("Did the 2025 Tahoe refresh change roof rack fit?",
  "Not in the data we read. Wikipedia describes the 2025 update as refreshed front and rear fascias with redesigned LED headlights and taillights, a 17.7 in screen inside, new 24 in wheels and the 3.0L Duramax on the Z71 for the first time. Nothing there touches the roof. The Rack Shop lists its Yakima and Z71 Thule kits for 2021–2026 as one span, Chevrolet Accessories lists 86558288 for 2021 through 2026, and four Amazon titles here run 2021–2026. The ROKIOTOEX title we list stops at 2025 and the EYOUHZ title at 2024, so owners of newer Tahoes should pick a listing that names their year or ask the seller."),
 ("Should I buy GM's own cross rails instead?",
  "If you want a dealer-installed, factory-look part, Chevrolet Accessories lists the Roof Rack Cross Rail Package in Black, part 86558288, for the 2021–2026 Suburban and Tahoe: aluminum, tie-down locations, removable for storage, dealer installation recommended, and a warranty of the balance of the bumper-to-bumper coverage or 12 months and 12,000 miles. The page does not print a load rating or a price we could read, so ask the dealer for both. We found no Amazon listing of this part that names the Tahoe, so it is not a pick here. Against the Thule and Yakima kits, you trade published ratings and a lifetime warranty for dealer backing."),
 ("Are the Amazon crossbars as good as Thule or Yakima?",
  "They cost a fraction of the price and publish a fraction of the proof. etrailer's Thule setup for the 2021 Tahoe is $704.85 with a limited lifetime warranty, a named fit kit and separate ratings for feet and bars. The Rack Shop's Yakima SightLine kit is $653.85 on sale. The Amazon sets here name the Tahoe and the years, print bar ratings up to 330 lb, and most say lockable, but we could not open an amazon.com page to read warranty terms or clamp details, and no maker page we found publishes them. For seasonal bikes and skis, the Amazon sets are a sensible buy if you recheck the clamps; for a heavy box left on all year, the brand-name kits are the safer money."),
 ("How far apart can I set the crossbars on a Tahoe?",
  "Farther than most boxes need. The Rack Shop lists a 58 in maximum bar spread for its Z71 Thule setup, and a 44 1/4 in crossbar spread for its Yakima SightLine kit. Yakima's and Thule's boxes in our cargo box guide ask for roughly 24 to 38 in, so the Tahoe's long roof is never the limit. Flush-rail feet and the Amazon clamps slide along the rail, so set the spread the carrier asks for, keep the front bar back from the sunroof opening, and leave room for the liftgate to swing."),
 ("Are these crossbars lockable?",
  "Most of the Amazon sets say so in the title: KINGGERI (\"Lockable\"), ROKIOTOEX (\"220LBs Lockable\"), EZREXPM (\"Lockable Crossbars\") and EYOUHZ (\"Adjustable Lockable\"). The BRIGHTLINES and ERKUL titles we read do not mention locks, and ASG Auto Sports sells BRIGHTLINES' Tahoe bars as anti-theft, so check the listing. On the brand-name kits, Thule and Yakima lock cores are sold separately. Locks stop someone lifting the set off a Tahoe in a parking lot; they do not make the bars theft-proof, and taking the bars off between trips also saves fuel."),
]

